cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis code or the derived data tables, please cite the archived release (version DOI below) and the associated article."
type: software
title: "Cross-platform transportability of a locked immune–metabolic transcriptional score for breast cancer overall survival"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a locked 14-gene immune-metabolic
  transcriptional score assessing cross-platform transportability in breast
  cancer overall survival. A score built in GSE42568 with frozen genes, Cox coefficients,
  training scaling and cutoff was applied once, without retraining, to three
  independent validation cohorts spanning two assay classes: GSE20685
  (Affymetrix microarray), SCAN-B GSE96058 (RNA-seq) and METABRIC (Illumina
  HT-12 microarray). The continuous per-SD association replicated in all three
  cohorts while the absolute cutoff did not transport. Exploratory five-class
  PAM50 heterogeneity in SCAN-B was not reproduced in the broader METABRIC
  CLAUDIN_SUBTYPE analysis.
